# Transient factory runtime state — not committed. The durable, reviewable artifacts
# (PLAN.md, config, schema, _workflow code, agents, verify, setup, templates) ARE committed;
# everything below is regenerable, and — per SETUP.md — is HOST data that must never enter
# this engine repo (KI-E26: findings name real systems, and the decision queue quotes
# customer-reported detail verbatim).
state/worktrees/
state/run-args.json
state/items/
state/normalized/
# Runtime markers/leases + --fresh backups (KI-C11 / KI-E6 / setup/init.mjs)
state/controller.json
state/STOP_REQUESTED.md
state/*.pre-fresh-*
# Host-local overrides (KI-E17 / SETUP.md § 6) — per-host, never committed
config/factory.config.local.json
verify/build-test.local.sh
# Repo style profiles (KI-E60) are HOST data — derived from each host's own private repos' PRs, the
# exact class KI-E26 keeps out of this engine repo. Only the README + the fictional example ship.
agents/repo-profiles/*
!agents/repo-profiles/README.md
!agents/repo-profiles/_example.Contoso.Widgets.md
telemetry/.env
telemetry/claude-code-telemetry.env
# Telemetry stream (KI-E7 / spine AD-8) — generated event data, never committed
telemetry/data/*
!telemetry/data/.gitkeep
# Per-host runtime artifacts (KI-E26) — the work items, the ledger, generated reports and the
# owner queue are the HOST's data, regenerated by `driver init` / `escalations` on every host.
state/ledger.json
state/findings-graph.json
state/PROGRESS.md
state/run-script*.js
state/results-*.json
reports/*
!reports/.gitkeep
queue/*
!queue/.gitkeep
# Claude Code session state (KI-E113) — per-host and/or generated, never engine content. Missed by
# the original KI-E26 sweep because `.claude/` is the one path that IS legitimately tracked in a
# HOST repo (its `.claude/rules/*.md` are the acceptance rules the factory enforces — that tracked
# copy is exactly what worktree.mjs's KI-L67 sparse-checkout strips out of each worktree). In THIS
# engine repo it is never engine content, for three separate reasons:
#   - `.claude/settings.local.json` is per-host session config; KI-E33/KI-E52 write the OTLP env
#     block (endpoints) into precisely this file.
#   - `.claude/worktrees/<branch>/` are REGISTERED git worktrees (`git worktree list`) — a full
#     checkout of this repo. Committing one is actively broken, not just noisy, and the Claude Code
#     worktree feature recreates them, so ignoring the contents once would not hold.
#   - `setup/init.mjs` INSTALLS the controller skill into `.claude/skills/`, so running init against
#     this repo (dogfooding) generates a copy of the tracked `claude-assets/` source. Committing the
#     copy would let it drift from the original it was generated from.
# The engine's own shipped Claude assets live in `claude-assets/` and ARE committed.
.claude/
